{# The Neighbourhood panel mount — the typed-link ring (hop 1) of the ref
   being read, grouped by ``ring_group`` heading. Lazy-loaded over HTMX
   from the ``/graph/{kind}/{id}/panel`` fragment so the page's cost stays
   one neighbourhood read, paid only when the panel renders. "graph ↗" is
   the slice-3 focus page; the two cross-link both ways
   (web-graph-navigation.md slices 2–3). One mount for every surface that
   wants the panel — today the shared ref detail template and the papers
   reader. #}
{% macro panel_mount(kind, ref_id) %}
<section class="mt-6" aria-label="Neighbourhood">
  <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 mb-2">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700">Neighbourhood</h2>
    <a href="/graph/{{ kind }}/{{ ref_id }}" class="text-xs text-sky-700 hover:underline">graph ↗</a>
  </div>
  <div id="graph-panel" hx-get="/graph/{{ kind }}/{{ ref_id }}/panel"
       hx-trigger="load" hx-swap="innerHTML">
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">loading neighbourhood…</p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endmacro %}
